# Deny-by-default. ~/.config holds 4.3 GB of application state; only the
# hand-built desktop shell belongs in here. Add a line to un-ignore, never
# rely on a blanket rule.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/eww/
!/hypr/
!/dunst/
!/wlogout/
!/rofi/
!/quickshell/
# torbik/ (the retired waybar) is left out on purpose since the public
# Ox Hyprland repo (2026-10-06): nothing at login loads it any more.

# Residue and generated state — never. These come last so they win over the
# un-ignores above. `~/` dirs are the XDG bug's leavings (a Brave profile, a
# VS Code session store, a PulseAudio auth cookie); `backup/` is the by-hand
# version control this repo replaces.
**/~/
**/__pycache__/
/backup/
/hypr.old/
/useless/

# Left out of the public Ox Hyprland repo (2026-10-06), kept on disk.
# The hyprlang tree is inert since the Lua conversion; its rollback is the
# old history (branch old-main), not files a reader would mistake for live.
/hypr/hyprland.conf
/hypr/conf/*.conf
# wlogout's suspend and hibernate icons: no button uses them and their
# origin is unknown. The four in use are Font Awesome Free (CC BY 4.0).
/wlogout/icons/**/suspend.png
/wlogout/icons/**/hibernate.png
